    "done_when": "Asserted in tests/test_pace_reads_the_lift.py through budget.group_pace and budget.pace_hold, every figure derived from fixtures at assertion time: with configured pace_multiple 1.1 and a codex-sub reading of utilisation 0.21 at 22.0 h of 168, an implement dispatch is held with no lift and admitted under a 1.8 lift anchored to the seven-day reset; it is held again once a reading's seven-day resets_at has moved; a drain-by lift granted at 21% holds at a reading above its line and admits at one below; an uncapped lift admits at any burn; a lift whose from is in the future is inert; a session lift admits that session's verdict and holds another session's on the same reading, with session threaded into group_pace and the preflight report as an optional argument; the preflight group entry carries the lifted multiple and the lift id; the readings history effective_budget receives comes from group_pace's records in observed order, as pace_replay reads rows, and pace_replay itself still reads the multiple each row recorded. In tests/test_pace_hold_releases_at.py, releases_at reads the banked-reset factor from where budget._scale_for_banked_reset records it rather than restating 2.0, and an allowance whose window cannot be placed yields releases_at None. Every test points RECKON_HOME at a temporary directory and asserts the real budget-lifts.json untouched. The declared negative control is applied on a scratch copy and the 1.8-lift admit assertion is observed red, the log's first line repeating the mutation verbatim. Gate: /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_pace_reads_the_lift.py tests/test_pace_hold_releases_at.py tests/test_budget_lift.py tests/test_pace.py tests/test_preflight_pace.py tests/test_pace_replay.py tests/test_burn_waits_for_a_readable_span.py tests/test_budget_window_length.py tests/test_picker_in_dispatch.py tests/test_picker_dispatch_pace.py tests/test_dispatch_records_the_pace_row.py, m